---
title: Project collection
layout: home
description: The page a portfolio opens on — who you are, what you have built, and the work itself as a grid of repo cards. The same page as a tag or a language filter, with a different list.
eyebrow: Collections · Project
source: src/components/repo-card.css · partials/components/repo-card.hbs
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Project · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>

	<div class="demo-controls">
		<p class="im-caption">Grid</p>
		<div class="im-btn-group" role="group" aria-label="Project grid"
			data-demo-target="#repos" data-demo-label="#repos-class">
			<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-demo-class="im-repos">Cards</button>
			<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button" data-demo-class="im-repos im-repos-list">List</button>
		</div>
		<code class="doc-source" id="repos-class" style="margin-left: auto"></code>
	</div>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap-wide" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1.75rem">
		<header class="im-collhead im-collhead-patterned">
			<span class="im-collhead-art im-bg-blueprint" style="--im-art: #3178c6" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			<p class="im-eyebrow">Work</p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Projects</h1>
			<p class="im-collhead-text">Things I have built and kept building. Everything here is open, and everything here is used by somebody — including me.</p>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta">
				<span>{{demo.projects.length}} repositories</span>
				<a href="#projects">4.2k stars</a>
				<a href="#projects">GitHub</a>
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="im-collbar">
			<div class="im-collbar-filters">
				<a class="im-tag" href="#projects" aria-current="page">All</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#projects">CSS</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#projects">TypeScript</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#projects">Handlebars</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#projects">Python</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#projects">Archived</a>
			</div>
			<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem">
				<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button">{{icon "list-filter"}}Most stars</button>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="im-repos" id="repos">
			{{#each demo.projects}}{{> "components/repo-card" cta=true}}{{/each}}
		</div>

		<div class="im-loadmore">
			<button class="im-btn" type="button">Load more</button>
			<p>6 of 24</p>
		</div>

		{{!-- A collection of projects is not only a grid of them: the writing about
		      the work belongs on the same page as the work. These are ordinary
		      POSTS, tagged, in the ordinary post card. --}}
		<section class="im-section">
			<div class="home-head"><p class="im-caption" data-index="log">From the project log</p><a class="im-card-cta" href="/collections/post/">All posts {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a></div>
			<div class="im-feed">
				{{#foreach demo.three}}{{> "components/post-card" excerpt=true}}{{/foreach}}
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail im-sticky-rail-full">
		<div class="im-widgets">
			<section class="im-widget im-widget-hire" aria-labelledby="jw-hire">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="jw-hire">Hire me</h2>
				<p class="im-widget-hire-state" data-state="available">Two days a week, from November</p>
				<ul class="im-widget-hire-list">
					<li>{{icon "component"}}<span>Design systems, and the Ghost themes on top of them.</span></li>
					<li>{{icon "gauge"}}<span>Making a slow site fast, with the numbers to show it.</span></li>
					<li>{{icon "users"}}<span>A week with your team, rather than a year of my invoices.</span></li>
				</ul>
				<a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-sm" href="#repos">{{icon "mail"}}Start a conversation</a>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="jw-sum">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="jw-sum">In total</h2>
				<div class="im-widget-stats">
					<div><strong>{{demo.projects.length}}</strong><span>Projects</span></div>
					<div><strong>4.1k</strong><span>Stars</span></div>
					<div><strong>4</strong><span>Live</span></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="jw-lang">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="jw-lang">Built with</h2>
				<span class="im-langbar">
					<span style="--im-repo-lang: var(--im-info); width: 44%"></span>
					<span style="--im-repo-lang: var(--im-accent); width: 31%"></span>
					<span style="--im-repo-lang: var(--im-success); width: 15%"></span>
					<span style="--im-repo-lang: var(--im-faint); width: 10%"></span>
				</span>
				<ul class="im-widget-list">
					<li><a href="#repos">TypeScript<small>44%</small></a></li>
					<li><a href="#repos">CSS<small>31%</small></a></li>
					<li><a href="#repos">Handlebars<small>15%</small></a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget im-rail-grow" aria-labelledby="jw-log">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="jw-log">The log <a href="/collections/project/log/">All</a></h2>
				<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-compact im-widget-series">
					{{#foreach demo.log}}
					<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="done">
						<span class="im-timeline-marker">{{@number}}</span>
						<h3 class="im-timeline-title"><a href="/collections/project/log/">{{title}}</a></h3>
					</li>
					{{/foreach}}
				</ol>
			</section>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>The same page as the post collection</h2>
		<p>A head, a bar of filters, a grid, a way to the next page. It is the <a href="/collections/post/">post collection</a> with a different card in the grid — <code>im-collhead</code>, <code>im-collbar</code> and the load-more are all the same components — and that is the point: a site where the writing and the work are laid out by two different sets of rules reads as two different sites.</p>
		<p>What changes is the <strong>card</strong>, because a project is not a post. A post wants a picture and an excerpt; a project wants a name, one line, what it is written in, how many people starred it and when it last moved. See <a href="/collections/project/card/">Project card</a>.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-repos</code></td><td>The grid. As many columns as fit at <code>--im-repos-min</code> (19rem).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-repos-list</code></td><td>One column. Pair it with <code>layout="bare"</code> on the cards and it becomes a ruled list — what a profile's repository tab looks like, and right for forty of them.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
		{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<div class="im-repos">
	{{#get "posts" filter="tag:project" limit="all"}}
		{{#foreach posts}}{{> "components/repo-card"}}{{/foreach}}
	{{/get}}
</div>
		{{{{/code}}}}
		<p>Ghost has no "repository" content type, so a theme builds one: a post tagged <code>#project</code>, with the numbers in its code injection or fetched once at build time from a host's public API. The card does not care where the data came from.</p>

		<h2>A ruled list instead</h2>
		<p><code>im-repos-list</code> with <code>layout="bare"</code>. No boxes, a rule between rows, and the whole thing reads as a table of contents rather than as a wall of cards.</p>
		{{#example}}
		<div class="im-repos im-repos-list">
			{{#each demo.projects}}{{#match @index "<" 3}}{{> "components/repo-card" layout="bare"}}{{/match}}{{/each}}
		</div>
		{{/example}}

		<h2>Pinned</h2>
		<p><code>layout="lg"</code>, in a two-column grid: the three or four you want looked at first, above everything else.</p>
		{{#example}}
		<div class="im-repos" style="--im-repos-min: 22rem">
			{{#each demo.projects}}{{#match @index "<" 2}}{{> "components/repo-card" layout="lg"}}{{/match}}{{/each}}
		</div>
		{{/example}}

		<h2>Details that matter</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>The owner is quiet and the name is not.</strong> <code>owner/<b>name</b></code> — one is context, one is the thing.</li>
			<li><strong>The language dot's colour comes from the data</strong>, not from a table in this repository. A design system has no business knowing about two hundred programming languages.</li>
			<li><strong>Archived is a state, not a strikethrough.</strong> <code>visibility="Archived"</code> tints the chip; the card is otherwise exactly as readable, because an archived project is still a project somebody may want.</li>
			<li><strong>The whole card is the link.</strong> The stars, the forks and the topics sit above that hit area, so they can go somewhere else.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
